### FILE generated/TUNING.md 2978
# Review & Tune (Before Apply)

This folder contains a **first draft** of:
- `masking_functions.sql` — masking UDFs + row filter functions
- `abac.auto.tfvars` — groups, tags, FGAC policies, and Genie agent config

Before you apply, tune for your business roles, security requirements, and Genie accuracy:

## Checklist — Genie Accuracy (review first)

- **Benchmarks**: Each benchmark question must be **unambiguous and self-contained**. The natural-language question and its ground-truth SQL must agree on the exact scope — e.g., "What is the average risk score for **active** customers?" (not "What is the average customer risk score?"). Run benchmarks in the Genie UI after apply to verify accuracy.
- **SQL filters**: Do the default WHERE clauses match your business definitions? (e.g., "active customers" = `CustomerStatus = 'Active'`, "completed transactions" = `TransactionStatus = 'Completed'`). These filters guide Genie's SQL generation.
- **SQL measures**: Are the standard metrics correct? (e.g., total revenue = `SUM(Amount)`, average risk = `AVG(RiskScore)`).
- **SQL expressions**: Are the computed dimensions useful? (e.g., transaction year, age bucket).
- **Join specs**: Do the join conditions between tables use the correct keys? Incorrect joins cause wrong results across all multi-table queries.
- **Instructions**: Does the instruction text define business defaults (e.g., "customer" means active by default) and domain conventions (date handling, metric calculations)?

## Checklist — ABAC & Masking

- **Groups and personas**: Do the groups map to real business roles?
- **Sensitive columns**: Are the right columns tagged (PII/PHI/financial/etc.)?
- **Masking behavior**: Are you using the right approach (partial, redact, hash) per sensitivity and use case?
- **Row filters and exceptions**: Are filters too broad/strict? Are exceptions minimal and intentional?

## Checklist — Genie agent Metadata & ACLs

- **Genie title & description**: Does the AI-generated title/description accurately represent the space?
- **Genie sample questions**: Do the sample questions reflect what business users will ask?
- **Per-space ACLs (`acl_groups`)**: Each space lists which groups get `CAN_RUN` access. Verify that:
  - Each space includes all groups that need access
  - Groups that should NOT see this space are excluded
  - Set durable per-agent `acl_groups` only on `genie_spaces[]` in `env.auto.tfvars`
  - Explicit `acl_groups = []` means nobody; omission derives fresh from policies (legacy mode only)
  - ACL fields in the generated draft are ignored
- **Validate before apply**: Run validation before `terraform apply`.

## Suggested workflow

1. Review and edit `masking_functions.sql` and `abac.auto.tfvars` in `generated/`.
2. Validate after each change:
   ```bash
   make validate-generated
   ```
3. When ready, apply (validates again, promotes shared account + workspace config, then runs terraform):
   ```bash
   make apply
   ```

### FILE generated/abac.auto.tfvars 10333
# ============================================================================
# GENERATED ABAC CONFIG (FIRST DRAFT)
# ============================================================================
# NOTE: Authentication comes from auth.auto.tfvars, environment from env.auto.tfvars.
# Tune the following before apply:
# - groups (business roles)
# - tag_assignments (what data is considered sensitive)
# - fgac_policies (who sees what, and how)
# Then validate before promoting into shared account + workspace config:
#   python validate_abac.py generated/abac.auto.tfvars generated/masking_functions.sql
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groups (business roles)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keys are group names. Use these to represent business personas (e.g., Analyst,
# Researcher, Compliance). These groups are used for workspace onboarding,
# Databricks One consumer access, data grants, and optional Genie agent ACLs.
#
# Docs:
# - Governed tags / tag policies: https://docs.databricks.com/en/database-objects/tags.html
# - Unity Catalog ABAC overview: https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac
# - ABAC policies (masks + filters): https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac/policies
# - Row filters + column masks: https://docs.databricks.com/en/tables/row-and-column-filters.html
#
groups = {
  "payments_ops" = { description = "Full access" }
  "viewers" = { description = "Masked" }
}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tag policies (governed tags)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each entry defines a governed tag key and the allowed values. You’ll assign
# these tags to tables/columns below, then reference them in FGAC policies.
#
# Docs:
# - Governed tags / tag policies: https://docs.databricks.com/en/database-objects/tags.html
# - Unity Catalog ABAC overview: https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac
# - ABAC policies (masks + filters): https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac/policies
# - Row filters + column masks: https://docs.databricks.com/en/tables/row-and-column-filters.html
#
tag_policies = [
  {
    key = "gr_treatment"
    description = "GenieRails-owned enforcement treatment derived from sensitivity findings. Entries are ordered strictest-first."
    values = ["redact", "compensation_redacted", "ssn_last4", "card_last4", "account_last4", "email_partial", "phone_partial", "name_partial", "date_year", "tfn_partial", "medicare_partial", "bsb_partial", "aadhaar_partial", "generic_partial", "round_amount"]
  }
]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tag assignments (classify tables/columns)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Apply governed tags to Unity Catalog objects.
# - entity_type: "tables" or "columns"
# - entity_name: fully qualified three-level name
#   - table:  "catalog.schema.Table"
#   - column: "catalog.schema.Table.Column"
# - Table-level tags are optional; use them to scope column masks or row filters
#   to specific tables, or for governance.
#
# Docs:
# - Governed tags / tag policies: https://docs.databricks.com/en/database-objects/tags.html
# - Unity Catalog ABAC overview: https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac
# - ABAC policies (masks + filters): https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac/policies
# - Row filters + column masks: https://docs.databricks.com/en/tables/row-and-column-filters.html
#
tag_assignments = [
  {
    entity_type = "columns"
    entity_name = "dev_fin.payments.customers.date_of_birth"
    tag_key = "gr_treatment"
    tag_value = "date_year"
  },
  {
    entity_type = "columns"
    entity_name = "dev_fin.payments.customers.email"
    tag_key = "gr_treatment"
    tag_value = "email_partial"
  },
  {
    entity_type = "columns"
    entity_name = "dev_fin.payments.customers.ssn"
    tag_key = "gr_treatment"
    tag_value = "ssn_last4"
  },
  {
    entity_type = "columns"
    entity_name = "dev_fin.payments.payments.cvv"
    tag_key = "gr_treatment"
    tag_value = "redact"
  }
]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FGAC policies (who sees what, and how)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each entry creates either a COLUMN MASK or ROW FILTER policy.
#
# Common fields:
# - name: logical name for the policy (must be unique)
# - policy_type: POLICY_TYPE_COLUMN_MASK | POLICY_TYPE_ROW_FILTER
# - catalog: catalog this policy is scoped to
# - function_catalog: catalog where the masking UDF lives
# - function_schema: schema where the masking UDF lives
# - to_principals: list of group names who receive this policy
# - except_principals: optional list of groups excluded (break-glass/admin)
# - comment: human-readable intent (recommended)
#
# For COLUMN MASK:
# - match_condition: ABAC condition, e.g. hasTagValue('phi_level','full_phi')
# - match_alias: the column alias used by the ABAC engine
# - function_name: masking UDF name (relative; Terraform prefixes catalog.schema)
# - when_condition: (optional) scope to specific tagged tables
#
# For ROW FILTER:
# - when_condition: (optional) scope to specific tagged tables
# - function_name: row filter UDF name (relative; must be zero-argument)
#
# Example — column mask (mask SSN for analysts, exempt compliance):
#   {
#     name              = "mask_ssn_analysts"
#     policy_type       = "POLICY_TYPE_COLUMN_MASK"
#     to_principals     = ["Junior_Analyst", "Senior_Analyst"]
#     except_principals = ["Compliance_Officer"]
#     comment           = "Mask SSN showing only last 4 digits"
#     match_condition   = "hasTagValue('pii_level', 'highly_sensitive')"
#     match_alias       = "masked_ssn"
#     function_name     = "mask_ssn"
#   }
#
# Example — row filter (restrict regional staff to their rows):
#   {
#     name           = "filter_us_region"
#     policy_type    = "POLICY_TYPE_ROW_FILTER"
#     to_principals  = ["US_Region_Staff"]
#     comment        = "Only show rows where region = US"
#     when_condition = "hasTagValue('region_scope', 'global')"
#     function_name  = "filter_by_region_us"
#   }
#
# Docs:
# - Governed tags / tag policies: https://docs.databricks.com/en/database-objects/tags.html
# - Unity Catalog ABAC overview: https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac
# - ABAC policies (masks + filters): https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac/policies
# - Row filters + column masks: https://docs.databricks.com/en/tables/row-and-column-filters.html
#
fgac_policies = [
  {
    name             = "gr_mask_dev_fin_redact"
    policy_type      = "POLICY_TYPE_COLUMN_MASK"
    catalog          = "dev_fin"
    to_principals    = ["viewers"]
    comment          = "GenieRails treatment redact; strictest-wins derivation"
    match_condition  = "hasTagValue('gr_treatment', 'redact')"
    match_alias      = "gr_treatment_redact"
    function_name    = "mask_redact"
    function_catalog = "dev_fin"
    function_schema  = "payments"
  },
  {
    name             = "gr_mask_dev_fin_ssn_last4"
    policy_type      = "POLICY_TYPE_COLUMN_MASK"
    catalog          = "dev_fin"
    to_principals    = ["viewers"]
    comment          = "GenieRails treatment ssn_last4; strictest-wins derivation"
    match_condition  = "hasTagValue('gr_treatment', 'ssn_last4')"
    match_alias      = "gr_treatment_ssn_last4"
    function_name    = "mask_redact"
    function_catalog = "dev_fin"
    function_schema  = "payments"
  },
  {
    name             = "gr_mask_dev_fin_email_partial"
    policy_type      = "POLICY_TYPE_COLUMN_MASK"
    catalog          = "dev_fin"
    to_principals    = ["viewers"]
    comment          = "GenieRails treatment email_partial; strictest-wins derivation"
    match_condition  = "hasTagValue('gr_treatment', 'email_partial')"
    match_alias      = "gr_treatment_email_partial"
    function_name    = "mask_email"
    function_catalog = "dev_fin"
    function_schema  = "payments"
  },
  {
    name             = "gr_mask_dev_fin_date_year"
    policy_type      = "POLICY_TYPE_COLUMN_MASK"
    catalog          = "dev_fin"
    to_principals    = ["viewers"]
    comment          = "GenieRails treatment fallback; principals are masking-only, not access scope"
    match_condition  = "hasTagValue('gr_treatment', 'date_year')"
    match_alias      = "gr_treatment_date_year"
    function_name    = "mask_date_to_year"
    function_catalog = "dev_fin"
    function_schema  = "payments"
  }
]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Genie agent configs (per-space semantic configuration)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each key is the human-readable space name matching genie_spaces[*].name in
